To implement the `queen_attack` logic, I will define a `chess_board` class 
within the `queen_attack` namespace. This class will store the positions of the 
white and black queens and provide a method to check if they can attack each 
other.



I'll update `queen_attack.h` to include the class definition and 
`queen_attack.cpp` to implement the constructor and the `can_attack` method. The
constructor will validate that the queens are on the board (0-7 for row and 
column) and not on the same square. The `can_attack` method will check if they 
share the same row, column, or diagonal.



queen_attack.h

```diff
@@ -1,8 +1,23 @@
