To calculate the minimum cost for the basket of books, we need to group the 
books into sets of distinct titles to maximize discounts. The greedy approach of
always taking the largest possible set of distinct books works, with one 
specific exception: a group of 5 and a group of 3 is more expensive than two 
groups of 4.



Here is the plan:

1.  Count the occurrences of each book title.

2.  Repeatedly form the largest possible group of distinct books from the 
remaining counts.

3.  Store the sizes of these groups.

4.  Apply the special rule: replace every pair of (group of 5, group of 3) with 
two groups of 4, because $2 \times \text{Cost}(4) < \text{Cost}(5) + 
\text{Cost}(3)$.

5.  Calculate the total cost based on the final group sizes.



book_store.go

