Ok, I will implement the `to_bytes` and `from_bytes` functions in `lib.rs` according to the VLQ encoding rules.

Here are the changes:
1.  `to_bytes`: Iterate through each `u32` value. For each value, extract 7-bit chunks from least significant to most significant. Store them in a temporary buffer. Then, reverse the buffer and set the continuation bit (bit 7) on all bytes except the last one. Append to the result.
2.  `from_bytes`: Iterate through the input bytes. Accumulate 7-bit chunks into a `u32` value. If the continuation bit is set, continue to the next byte. If it's clear, we've finished a number, so push it to the result list. If we reach the end of the byte stream and the last number was incomplete (continuation bit was set on the last byte processed), return `Error::IncompleteNumber`.

lib.rs
```
#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Error {
    IncompleteNumber,
}

/// Convert a list of numbers to a stream of bytes encoded with variable length encoding.
pub fn to_bytes(values: &[u32]) -> Vec<u8> {
    let mut result = Vec::new();
    for &value in values {
        if value == 0 {
            result.push(0);
            continue;
        }

        let mut buffer = Vec::new();
        let mut v = value;
        while v > 0 {
            buffer.push((v & 0x7F) as u8);
            v >>= 7;
        }

        // The buffer has the chunks in reverse order (LSB first)
        // We need to output them MSB first, with continuation bits set appropriately.
        for (i, byte) in buffer.iter().rev().enumerate() {
            if i < buffer.len() - 1 {
                result.push(byte | 0x80);
            } else {
                result.push(*byte);
            }
        }
    }
    result
}

/// Given a stream of bytes, extract all numbers which are encoded in there.
pub fn from_bytes(bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<Vec<u32>, Error> {
    let mut result = Vec::new();
    let mut current_value: u32 = 0;
    let mut in_sequence = false;

    for &byte in bytes {
        in_sequence = true;
        current_value = (current_value << 7) | (byte & 0x7F) as u32;

        if byte & 0x80 == 0 {
            // End of a number
            result.push(current_value);
            current_value = 0;
            in_sequence = false;
        }
    }

    if in_sequence {
        return Err(Error::IncompleteNumber);
    }

    Ok(result)
}
